What:           /sys/bus/serial/devices/.../event
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Read-only SY108 MCU event snapshot. It reports "none" before
                any event, otherwise "seq=<number> kind=poweroff|usb-reset".
                A power request awaiting orderly shutdown takes precedence
                over the latest USB event, including during early boot.

                The driver emits a change uevent with MCU_EVENT and MCU_SEQ.
                USB ACKs are sent by the driver before the uevent. A pending
                power ACK is attempted only from the SYS_POWER_OFF blocking
                reboot notifier, before UART device shutdown. There is no
                userspace ACK attribute. A restart does not send a power ACK.

What:           /sys/bus/serial/devices/.../firmware_version
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Read-only MCU firmware version returned by the UART protocol.
                A transport error is returned to the reader.

What:           /sys/bus/serial/devices/.../status
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Read-only transport counters, including received frames,
                protocol errors, ADC requests, timeouts, MCU events and ACK
                attempts. last_ack_error is the result of the last UART write.
                A completed write and transmit drain do not prove receipt by
                the MCU. ADC3..5 use the standard IIO raw voltage attributes.
